.TH CTLYRICS 1 "September 2026" "ctlyrics 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctlyrics \- terminal lyrics viewer and mapping manager for cmus
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctlyrics
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B ctlyrics web
.RI [ --bind address ]
.RI [ --port port ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctlyrics
starts cmus in an embedded pseudoterminal when needed, reads its playback
information, and displays synchronized LRC lyrics. Press Ctrl+W to switch
between the full-screen cmus and lyrics interfaces. The embedded cmus process
exits together with ctlyrics. The program also provides desktop tray
integration and a local Web interface for managing lyric mappings.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show command help.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Show the program version.
.TP
.BI "--lang " language
Set the interface language to auto, en, or zh-CN.
.SH WEB OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--bind " address
Address to listen on. The default is 127.0.0.1. Use 0.0.0.0 only when network
access is explicitly required.
.TP
.BR -p , " --port " port
Port to listen on. The default is 3000.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Ctrl+W
Switch between the embedded cmus and lyrics interfaces.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Quit safely and restore the terminal state from either interface.
.TP
.B q
Quit ctlyrics from the lyrics interface. In the cmus interface, keys other than
the global Ctrl+W and Ctrl+C shortcuts are passed to cmus.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ctlyrics/mappings.json
Music directory and lyric mappings.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ctlyrics/language
Saved TUI and CLI language preference.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/ctlyrics/lyrics/
LRC lyric files.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/ctlyrics/
Application logs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cmus (1),
.BR cmus-remote (1)
